            <div xml:id="d53">

                <pb facs="0042" n="38" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg38"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">600.939/239: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-08-11T19:00:00-04:00">August 11, 1938—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>281. Your 520, August 8, 3 p.m., via Tientsin.<anchor n="57" xml:id="d53-f1"/> In
                    the light of Tientsin’s 154, August 10, 3 p.m.,<anchor n="57" xml:id="d53-f2"/>
                    the Department suggests that in your discretion you defer further action for a
                    few days pending a clarification of the situation. If in your opinion action
                    should then still be considered desirable, you may use your discretion with
                    reference to the contents of the proposed <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >aide-mémoire</hi>.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
